                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June 21,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 727.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to ackowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 1413, of the 11th instant, on the subject of the arrest and imprisonment of
                    Nathaniel F. Bonsall.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have to inform you that, from the appearance of the case as it is now
                    before the Department, it is not perceived that an}’ further action can be
                    taken.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
